{"content": "Here is a regular expression that matches a valid IPv4 address:\n\n```regex\n^(?:(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9]?[0-9])\\.){3}(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9]?[0-9])$\n```\n\n### Explanation of Each Part\n\nThis regex is constructed by validating a single number between 0 and 255 and applying it to four octets separated by dots.\n\n1.  **`^` and `$`**:\n    *   Anchors that ensure the entire string matches the pattern from start to finish. Without them, the regex might match a substring inside a longer number (e.g., matching `192.168.1.1` inside `192.168.1.1abc`).\n\n2.  **`(?: ... )` (Non-capturing Group)**:\n    *   This groups the logic for a single valid number (0\u2013255) without creating a backreference capture group", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.048411644903332274, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.048411644903332274}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -3.2631943597470823}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -5.656466759649426}, {"token": "```", "logprob": -5.919894494024426}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -6.33720139404884}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -8.451869286504895}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -9.083548821417004}, {"token": "`", "logprob": -9.24134186646095}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -9.427666939703137}, {"token": "Regular", "logprob": -9.62334755798927}, {"token": "One", "logprob": -9.706946648565442}, {"token": "An", "logprob": -9.90461853882423}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -10.033637322393567}, {"token": "No", "logprob": -10.17983940979591}, {"token": "This", "logprob": -10.322543419805676}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -10.701844490972668}, {"token": "Regex", "logprob": -11.019666947332531}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -11.082995690313489}, {"token": "While", "logprob": -11.16128758331886}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -11.670293129888684}]}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -8.356551635202436e-05, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " is", "logprob": -8.356551635202436e-05}, {"token": " are", "logpr