{"content": "To find files larger than 100MB under the `/var` directory, the standard `find` command approach is:\n\n```bash\nsudo find /var -type f -size +100M\n```\n\n*(Note: `sudo` is included because many files under `/var` require elevated permissions to read.)*\n\n### Flag Explanation\n\nHere is a breakdown of what each flag does:\n\n| Flag | Value | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `find` | N/A | The command used to locate files based on criteria. |\n| `/var` | N/A | The directory path to search starting from this root. |\n| `-type f` | `f` | Restricts the search to **files only** (excluding directories, symlinks, or devices). Without this, `find` might attempt to report directories. |\n| `-size +100M` | `+100M` | Filters for files **larger** than the specified size.<br>\u2022 `+` means \"greater than\".<br>\u2022 `100` is the numeric value.<br>\u2022 `M` stands for Megabytes (you could", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "To", "logprob": -1.6828957998080654, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.43123259180025286}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -1.6828957998080654}, {"token": "```", "logprob": -2.0812303029818935}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -3.6538735830111904}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -4.845609804324667}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -5.9750062429233}, {"token": "`", "logprob": -6.080402513675253}, {"token": "bash", "logprob": -8.609167238406698}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -8.755268236331503}, {"token": "B", "logprob": -9.226913591556112}, {"token": "Use", "logprob": -9.246105333499472}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -9.260980745486776}, {"token": "First", "logprob": -10.178159853152792}, {"token": "`,", "logprob": -10.27006067865328}, {"token": "Command", "logprob": -10.345938821963827}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -10.5766908132358}, {"token": "to", "logprob": -10.744995256595175}, {"token": "One", "logprob": -10.890571733645956}, {"token": " Here", "logprob": -11.021252771548788}, {"token": "Find", "logprob": -11.2291432821078